# FURUI 0.2.8 on ordinary text in five languages other than English: the plan, anchored before the run

**Status:** a plan record. It fixes the sentences, the version and the lines before any AI stage is called on them. The result is corrective information for FURUI; it is not used to claim that any bar was passed.

    sentences          2,000: German, Spanish, Chinese (simplified), Arabic and Hindi, two sets of 200 each per language: Wikipedia articles on AI at fixed revisions, and text written by users (for German, news articles instead)
    sets               de_wiki, de_news, es_wiki, es_user, zh_wiki, zh_user, ar_wiki, ar_user, hi_wiki, hi_user
    file sha256        44ed7a3037d8d1e57ea9c088d37d6fa8359a69cbaf092ff10f66dd578d0658ca (the sentences are not published)
    manifest sha256    97f21ba7a7fd1d02829dfef7e2785289496781752b5d7af4eb8746ce0e31e465
    sources sha256     e4a03de73447ccac1ee20e7e78e19355b9defaabd4fa13d22f0de244af06d28f
    lines sha256       3b1c9f062faaae6c639bc769cb1f37d35a4958c2e7c3d180f69de53379717bdb
    run tool sha256    201a209bbd9cfe036e0ecb2a80c822b2c3bf355e4dbbd9322ea451591dac09be
    version            FURUI 0.2.8: the rules, then claude-haiku-5-5, then claude-opus-5-5 on what the first stage did not pass, prompt v1 as pinned for blind-02 (BLIND02_PIN.json sha256 5cf6fe65a0c203a8fb52e13c59d4e5ce2f3ec1cb04be2757e04df39db02d0f8d)
    lines              per set of 200: at most 4 wrongly refused, counted fail-closed; no API refusal. Counted strictly as well. A language with any API refusal is reported as one where FURUI can give no answer.
    notes              de_news is news articles, not text written by users, so German has no set of user-written text; es_user was rejoined from CoNLL tokens, so spacing around punctuation may differ from the original text; hi_user does not state on its card whether it was written or translated, and is not presented as representative of Hindi text written by users.

**The SHA-256 of this document is anchored to the JIDEC ledger and stamped to Bitcoin. After anchoring, this record cannot be altered. Corrections are later entries that cite this one.**
